result_location:pass("Theorem 4.2 bound clause is at lines 870–874, Theorem 4.3 at 942–950, Theorem 5.1 at 1332–1336, and Theorems 6.3–6.5 at 1986–2043. These are proved results of this primary edition; in particular (6.22) is the actual Theorem 6.5, not its earlier forward reference.",[`${bit}:870-874`,`${bit}:942-950`,`${bit}:1332-1336`,`${bit}:1986-2049`]),
statement_fidelity:pass("E001(i) retains sigma>=0, the initial L2 bound and all bound dependencies from (4.13). Clause (ii) retains sigma>0, 0<rho<sigma, fixed 1<p<infinity, strong and weak-* convergence, the limiting bound and a.e. conservation. Clause (iii) retains the separate >1/2, (0,1/2], and zero cases, continuous representatives, uniqueness and data dependence; all-time conservation at low positive order and smooth approximation at zero are explicit in the source context. Clause (iv) reproduces -1<theta<=0, the sum bound on the two initial L2 norms and C'(B0,theta) C_(B0,theta)^b. The source H^rho on mean-zero inputs is topologically equivalent to D003's inhomogeneous norm. No strengthened ball uniformity or project convergence theorem is imported.",["nl0.json#/propositions/3/statement",`${bit}:243-268`,`${bit}:870-881`,`${bit}:942-950`,`${bit}:1478-1490`,`${bit}:1551-1563`,`${bit}:1986-2043`]),
