const structure=pass("Compared the exhaustive overview with the canonical statements and every R input/output edge. The bound hashes are spec.json=c4b96c3fff4ea12b6aae65fc0149620e5bf65fe76e0a9c40f1c608fc9c814cd1 and nl0.json=d5215cd0e88e2d14678ef4f7f0fb9c73a2613a9b28cad3ce02c8cc00738053e7; nl0.spec_sha256 matches. H001–H003 exactly retain T>0, 0<gamma<=1, R>0; all are in P's closure, with no unused original H. The datum's reality, zero mean, H^gamma ball and positive integral step count remain universal antecedents in P rather than new roots. All 20 propositions are in the target closure: the only roots are H001–H003 and E001–E005. Each of N001–N011 and P has exactly one producer R001–R012, all inputs are present and earlier, and there is no cycle or alternative-producer/OR interpretation. R003,R004,R006 have empty premise lists but remain internal proved lemmas, not assumptions. All 21 D entries match their canonical records, have earlier definition dependencies and introduce no extra graph roots. In particular D020 does not assume a solution exists; N001 exports existence/bounds. D013 postpones bounded extension to N005, D015/D019 to N006, D008 well-definedness and D021 compatibility to N007. The exported N statements preserve the supplied covariance/two-ratio and third-largest-frequency route (N003–N005), continuous-source bridge (N002), stepwise interpolation/residual (N006–N009), both-endpoint low/high stability (N010), restart/bootstrap (N011), then fixed-step density (P). The fixed Scheme has no frequency cutoff. This PASS concerns the graph and faithful exports; it does not certify any R body or per-consumer source application, which require their independent local assessments.",
